{"question_id": "6b7dfb22", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on what's in your history, here are some ideas tailored to you:\n\n- **Step away from the feed.** Your inspiration has mostly come from social media, especially Instagram flower paintings — try observing real flowers instead: pick up a bouquet, visit a garden, or sketch from life, which also supports your goal of painting realistic flowers.\n- **Theme your 30-day challenge.** You recently started a 30-day painting challenge, so give each day a constraint: one flower species, a limited palette, or a \"texture day\" using the palette knife techniques you were exploring.\n- **Play with texture as the spark.** You've been wanting to incorporate more texture — swapping brushes for a palette knife (impasto, scraping, swirling) can shake up your usual approach and generate new ideas.\n- **Break it down and track it.** You already planned to split projects into smaller tasks with deadlines; also track your progress and celebrate small milestones, since you tend to lose steam midway.\n- **Cross-pollinate subjects.** While acrylics and flowers are your focus, painting the same flower in different styles (loose vs. realistic, monochrome, exaggerated color) can feel fresh without abandoning what you like.", "n_records": 20, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 3419, "completion_tokens": 1500, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|art_medium_interest", "assistant|acrylic_paint_brand_recommendations", "assistant|acrylic_brush_brand_recommendations", "self|instagram_inspiration", "self|painting_subject_interest", "assistant|flower_painting_tips", "self|texture_goal", "assistant|palette_knife_techniques", "self|online_selling_intent", "assistant|artwork_pricing_tips", "self|artwork_photography_struggle", "assistant|artwork_photography_tips", "self|studio_space_plan", "assistant|studio_setup_tips", "self|focus_problem", "self|inspiration_source", "self|painting_challenge", "assistant|motivation_tips", "self