{"question_id": "d24813b1", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Since your lemon poppyseed cake was a hit with colleagues before, a lemon-based cake is a safe bet — and you've already flagged the Lemon Lavender Pound Cake as interesting. For that one, use 1 tsp dried lavender buds (you decided on buds rather than syrup or infused milk), bake at 325°F (165°C) for 55–60 minutes in a 9x5-inch loaf pan, and start with a small amount of lavender so it doesn't overpower the cake.\n\nIf you want a second item, you've already considered bringing chocolate chip cookies to a party — the chewy recipe (375°F / 190°C for 10–12 minutes) works well, and key tips are room-temperature butter, not overmixing the dough, not overbaking, and chilling the dough first.\n\nOne thing to check before deciding: any colleagues' personal preferences or dietary restrictions, since that should guide the final recipe choice.", "n_records": 55, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 5362, "completion_tokens": 1444, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|baking_request", "self|birthday_cake_plan", "self|lemon_poppyseed_cake_history", "self|flavor_preference", "self|lavender_choice", "self|party_plan", "assistant|recipe_chocolate_cake", "assistant|recipe_chocolate_cake_ingredients", "assistant|recipe_chocolate_cake_baking", "assistant|recipe_caramel_ganache", "assistant|baking_tip", "assistant|lemon_cake_suggestion", "assistant|party_suggestion", "assistant|lavender_option", "assistant|lavender_method", "assistant|lavender_tip", "assistant|recipe_lemon_lavender_cake", "assistant|recipe_lemon_lavender_cake_baking", "assistant|recipe_lemon_lavender_cake_sugar", "assistant|recipe_lemon_lavender_cake_lemon", "assistant|recipe_lemon_lavender_cake_lavender", "assistant|cake_storage", "assistant|cake_storage_tip", "assistant|cake_serving_tip", "assistant|cookie_tip", "assistant|recipe_chocolate_chip_cookies", "assistant|recipe_chocolate_chip_cookies_baking"], "digest_bytes": 7304}
