{"question_id": "b6025781", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Since you've already done grilled chicken and turkey breast, here are new ideas for next week (week of June 5) based on your quinoa + roasted veg setup:\n\n**New proteins to try**\n- **Lentil & mushroom bolognese** — you've never tried it, and it meal-preps beautifully: sauté onion/garlic/carrot/celery, add mushrooms, lentils, crushed tomatoes and basil/oregano, simmer 20–25 min (30–40 min total, 4–6 servings). Make a double batch and freeze up to 3 months.\n- **Pan-seared salmon** with lemon, salt and pepper — omega-rich and fast.\n- **Marinated baked or pan-fried tofu** (or crumbled) — plant-based, takes on the Classic Herbs flavors you like.\n- **Chickpea salad with a tangy dressing** — no cooking required.\n- **Shrimp sautéed with garlic, lemon and herbs** — quick-cooking, good fresh or reheated.\n- **Edamame** steamed with salt, pepper and chili flakes, or **marinated tempeh** — easy plant-based sides.\n- **Grilled steak, sliced** — if you want a red-meat option.\n\n**Sides that use what you have**\n- **Roasted sweet potatoes with fresh rosemary** — uses the rosemary in your fridge and matches your Classic Herbs pick: 425°F/220°C, 20–25 min, flipping halfway.\n- **Roasted broccoli with garlic and lemon**, or **sautéed greens** (spinach with garlic and lemon; kale with cherry tomatoes and balsamic).\n\n**Snack**\n- Your planned **homemade granola** — customize with cinnamon, almonds/chia, and dried cranberries; go light on the honey/maple syrup if you want it less sweet.\n\n**Prep flow:** roast a big vegetable batch on the weekend (holds ~5 days in the fridge) and cook one large batch of quinoa to portion out for the week.", "n_records": 44, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 4829, "completion_tokens": 2716, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|meal_prep_habit", "self|protein_sources_tried", "self|lentil_bolognese_experience", "self|meal_prep_plan", "self|seasoning_preference", "self|fridg